  "id": "survivor-guilt",
  "term": "survivor guilt",
  "definition": "Survivor guilt is a form of self-directed distress in which a person has negative thoughts and feelings about having survived when others did not, or about not being seriously injured when others were. In the PTSD literature in this packet, it is described as an associated feature rather than a core diagnostic criterion.",
